~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
[EXPLAIN] What this step does
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
  Uses the trained model from step 04 to predict how strongly each FDA-approved drug would inhibit
  the parasite enzyme         TgDHFR (Toxoplasma gondii dihydrofolate reductase), without doing
  any lab work (virtual screening).
  1) Load the model. 2) Learn what the training molecules look like and flag drugs that are too
  different from them         (Applicability Domain, via an Isolation Forest): the model is only
  trustworthy for molecules similar to those it was         trained on, so unusual drugs are
  dropped instead of receiving a made-up prediction. 3) Drop drugs that are very large         (MW
  above the limit) or contain atoms outside the allowed set (H, C, N, O, F, P, S, Cl, Br, I). 4)
  Predict pIC50.         5) Report and export the ranking.
  pIC50 = -log10(IC50 in molar). Higher means more potent: 6 is IC50 = 1 uM, 7 is 100 nM, 8 is 10
  nM.         Candidates are later confirmed by docking (step 07) and filtered for drug-
  likeness/safety (step 08).
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

