~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
[EXPLAIN] Report B: ranking and efficiency metrics
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
  Besides predicted potency (pIC50), the table gives metrics that judge whether the potency is
  'earned' efficiently:         LE (ligand efficiency) = potency per heavy atom, >= 0.3 is
  generally considered good; BEI = potency per kDa of mass;         LLE = pIC50 minus logP, >= 5
  suggests potency is not just coming from greasiness (lipophilicity); SEI = potency per
  polar surface area. A high pIC50 with poor LE/LLE usually means a big or greasy molecule that is
  a weaker lead.
