~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
[EXPLAIN] What this figure shows
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
  R2 on the held-out test molecules for the experiments of step 04 (A baseline, B + feature
  selection, C +         augmentation), each with its 95% bootstrap confidence interval, next to
  the values reported in the original paper         (dashed lines). Intervals that overlap are not
  statistically distinguishable: with a small test set, apparent         gains from feature
  selection or augmentation are often within noise. The two hollow points on the right are
  diagnostics: the same B and C, but with the bits selected using the test set (as in the original
  study). They are         optimistically biased, and the gap to B and C shows how much that leak
  can inflate the score.
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
